  "result": "I added `clamp(cents, low, high)` to `shop/money.py` with tests, and the full suite passes: 12 tests, `OK`, run with `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -t .`.\n\n- **Behaviour:** values below `low` come back as `low` and values above `high` come back as `high`. Anything in between is returned unchanged. `low > high` raises `ValueError`, and `low == high` is allowed and returns that value.\n- **No type checks:** nothing else in `money.py` checks argument types, so `clamp` doesn't either.\n- **Tests:** there was no test file for `money.py`, so I created `tests/test_money.py`, written like `tests/test_pricing.py`. It covers inside the range, below, above, exactly at each bound, `low == high`, and `low > high`.\n\nNothing is committed.",
